{"id": "dc98e0b6-6ae7-48cf-8851-cd2834229694", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:47:26.372168", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-23T12:46\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "9c334993-0f59-47dd-8276-e440081806e0", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T12:47:26.374781", "source": "user", "parent_id": "dc98e0b6-6ae7-48cf-8851-cd2834229694", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Before we commit to anything, please do a scoping pass only — no full design yet.\\n\\n1) Input inspection: confirm what actually exists in /workspace (any codebase, config, data, or prior notes relevant to a targeted-molecule generation pipeline with property feedback). Report what is present and, explicitly, what is absent. Do not assume a model, dataset, or reward implementation exists unless you can point to it.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach outline (not the finished deliverable): sketch how you would structure a design-only experiment that tests whether embedding a chemical-feedback loop built on p-logP, QED and a binding-affinity proxy (a) improves property scores, (b) reduces \\\"molecular hallucination\\\" (invalid/unvalisable or off-distribution structures), and (c) preserves structural diversity and realistic structural distributions rather than degenerating into artefacts such as over-represented ultra-long carbon chains. In the sketch, name the comparison arms you would use (feedback-off baseline, feedback-on, and any intermediate/ablated variant), the kind of control that isolates the feedback loop itself from confounders such as extra sampling compute, fine-tuning steps, or simple filtering/rejection sampling against the same property functions, and the headline metric families you would report.\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties you want me to rule on, for example: what stands in for \\\"binding affinity\\\" if no docking/scoring tool is available in this environment (the runtime here has no network and no preinstalled cheminformatics or docking stack — treat tool availability as an open question, not a given); what target/task setting is assumed for \\\"targeted molecule discovery\\\"; what reference \\\"real-world distribution\\\" you would compare against (e.g. a curated public corpus such as ChEMBL/PC/SMILES-like training data) given that no datasets are declared in this project; the validity metric for hallucination (canonicalisability, valence/chemistry checks, scaffold uniqueness, fragment plausibility); and the diversity statistic you would use (e.g. scaffold/framework entropy, nearest-neighbour Tanimoto distance distribution, internal diversity) rather than a single scalar.\\n\\nKeep this to inspection plus a short approach proposal and the list of decisions you need from me. Do not produce the final design, controls table, or analysis plan in this turn.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"Incorporating the chemical feedback mechanism, which leverages properties such as p-logP, QED, and binding affinity, directly improves the generation of molecules with superior chemical properties and reduces molecular hallucinations in targeted molecule discovery tasks. Does embedding this feedback loop better align molecule generation with real-world distributions, preserving structural diversity (e.g., avoiding over-representation of ultra-long carbon chains) while enhancing property scores?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
