ctives set A_t**: ChEMBL activities with assay confidence \\u2265 6, direct-type assays (B/F), pChEMBL \\u2265 6.0; deduplicated molecules; capped at 2,000 largest-potency representatives per target. **If |A_t| < 100 after filtering, target t is excluded from the panel and the exclusion reported.**\\n- **s_aff(m; t)** = max Tanimoto(ECFP4(m), ECFP4(a)) over a \\u2208 A_t. ECFP4 = Morgan radius 2, 2048 bits, RDKit defaults, chirality off, fixed a priori. Invalid m \\u2192 s_aff undefined \\u2192 contributes via R=0 rule. Ties: irrelevant to max; for any top-K selection, ties broken by ascending canonical SMILES (deterministic).\\n- **Secondary/speculative**: PR7 learned predictor as s_aff; **no headline conclusion loads on it**; if PR7 absent, the similarity-transfer result stands with the stated proxy-validity limitation (\\\"proxy rewards structural resemblance to known actives, not physical binding\\\"). **No docking is performed or claimed.**\\n\\n## 6. Arms\\n\\n| Arm | Description | What it isolates |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **A0** | Base checkpoint + U reward-free self-training updates (identical pipeline to A1; candidates drawn identically but *uniformly* selected, no R) | extra gradient steps / self-training drift / decode budget |\\n| **A1** | Full feedback loop (R = w\\u00b7(p-logP, QED, s_aff)) | the loop |\\n| **A2** | A0 generator, N_pool draws, keep top-K by the *same* R; invalid excluded from ranking but counted (\\u00a78 table) | feedback \\u2248 filtering? |\\n| **A3** | A1 pipeline with R replaced by per-sample-permuted A1-reward values (identical weight distribution, zero information) | reward information vs. mechanics |\\n| **A4a/A4b** | Loop with (w1,w2,0) property-only / (0,0,1)-style affinity-only | component attribution |\\n| **A1p** (conditional on PR6) | Pretrained-checkpoint version of A0/A1/A2 triplet | prior-strength robustness (D3) |\\n| **A1\\u2032** | Target-agnostic condition (w3 = 0, no target) | \\\"targeted\\\" vs generic property optimisation |\\n| Grid G | A1/A2 re-run under \\u00a79 weightings | researcher-choice sensitivity |\\n\\n## 7. Compute-matching protocol (explicit, per additional requirement)\\n\\n1. **Decode budget**: every arm draws exactly N = 100,000 candidate molecules [est] per (seed, target) for final evaluation; A1's training draws are logged separately.\\n2. **Gradient updates**: A0 and A3 execute the *same* U updates, batch size, optimiser state, LR schedule, and candidate draws M per update as A1; only the selection weights differ (uniform / permuted / R-weighted).\\n3. **A2 cost logging**: N_pool required to fill top-K is logged per arm; A2's N_pool is additionally matched to A1's total training draws (with replacement noted if pool exhausted). A reviewer can therefore see A2 gets \\u2265 A1's sampling compute, and A0/A3 get A1's full update count.\\n4. All arms share RNG streams, decoding temperature, and the same fixed output size **K = 10,000** [est] molecules (D5 fixed-K subsampling; deterministic seed).\\n\\n## 8. Metrics, denominators, and exclusion rules (D4/D5 \\u2014 no arm may shrink its own denominator)\\n\\n| Family | Metrics | Denominator policy (fixed) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Property (P) | QED, SA (RDKit sascorer), p-logP window score, composite R, success-rate at pre-set thresholds | reported on **all K outputs**, invalid scored 0; secondary valid-only view shown side-by-side |\\n| Hallucination (H) | (i) parse/sanitisation/canonicalisation failure rate; (ii) valence & ring-size (3\\u20138) violations; (iii) duplicate rate post-canonicalisation (uniqueness); (iv) off-distribution rate: log-frequency under corpus fragment (fixed-size circular fragments) and generic-Murcko-scaffold frequency models \\u2014 molecule scored by mean min-log-prob; (v) artifact detector: max contiguous aliphatic-C run \\u2265 L*, L* = corpus 99.5th percentile fixed from PR3 before any arm runs | **all K outputs, always**; unparseable outputs retained (they *are* the hallucination signal) |\\n| Diversity (D) | ECFP4 NN-Tanimoto distance distribution, internal diversity (mean pairwise Tanimoto complement), generic-scaffold count + Shannon entropy of scaffold distribution | fixed-K samples; distributions reported, never a lone scalar |\\n| Alignment (A) | FDD-style descriptor-distribution distance vs reference; Morgan-density and scaffold JS divergence; principal-moments-of-inertia shape plot vs reference; chain-length, heavy-atom, ring-count histograms vs reference tails | fixed-K samples vs fixed reference (\\u00a74) |\\n\\n**Caveat (required, D3/D4):** with a from-scratch generator, baseline invalid/off-distribution rates are expected to be high, giving the loop visible headroom; the A1p sensitivity triplet and explicitly reported baseline rates let the reader judge how much of any \\\"gain\\\" is headroom exploitation. If PR6 is unavailable, this remains a limitation, not a result.\\n\\n## 9. Weighting sensitivity (w1/w2/w3 is a researcher choice \\u2014 probed, not hidden)\\n\\nPre-registered grid of 5 weightings: (\\u2153,\\u2153,\\u2153) primary; (.2,.5,.3); (.3,.2,.5); (.5,.3,.2); (.1,.3,.6) [affinity-heavy]. Headline contrast patterns (below) are recomputed per weighting; the headline conclusion is only declared *stable* if its category is unchanged in \\u2265 4/5 weightings; otherwise the conclusion is reported as weighting-dependent.\\n\\n## 10. Pre-registered decision criteria (patterns; no prediction of which obtains)\\n\\nAll contrasts per (seed, target) across 5 training seeds [est]; seed-level paired bootstrap/permutation tests (p < 0.05, BH-corrected across families) with effect sizes and seed SDs reported. Let \\u0394(X) denote arm X \\u2212 baseline on a metric family.\\n\\n- **\\\"Loop adds something beyond filtering\\\"**: \\u0394(A1\\u2212A0) favours A1 on H and (P), **and** \\u0394(A1\\u2212A2) is positive on \\u2265 1 alignment metric and on off-distribution rate with CI excluding 0, **and** \\u0394(A1\\u2212A3) favours A1 on H \\u2014 i.e., gains not reproduced by same-reward filtering or same-mechanics noise \\u2014 **and** diversity trio for A1 non-inferior to A0 (NN-Tanimoto and scaffold entropy CIs within a pre-set non-inferiority margin of seed SD).\\n- **\\\"Loop \\u2261 filtering\\\"**: A2 \\u2248 A1 on all four families (all CIs crossing 0), with both beating A0/A3. The loop's extra machinery buys nothing over ranking.\\n- **\\\"Loop degrades diversity/alignment\\\"**: A1 wins (P) and possibly (H) but fails the diversity non-inferiority clause or shows alignment regression (e.g., scaffold entropy collapse, chain-run tail vs corpus) \\u2014 including any ultra-long-chain artifact spike in A1 but not A2 (signature of reward hacking).\\n- **\\\"Null\\\"**: A1 \\u2248 A0 on (P) and (H) across seeds.\\n- **\\\"Mixed\\\"**: any pattern outside the above four; reported as-is with the failing contrast named. Weighting sensitivity (\\u00a79) and A1p (if available) qualify the category, never overwrite it.\\n\\n## 11. Feasibility (explicit)\\n\\n- **Verified absent in the current container** (inspection, 2026-10-23): RDKit, numpy/scipy/pandas/torch, any docking/scoring tool, any dataset or checkpoint, pip cache, and *network access itself* (DNS resolution fails; pip download fails). Python 3.14 only, CPU-only (224 cores, no GPU). **Nothing in this design was executed here, and none of it is executable here as-is.**\\n- Runnable elsewhere as specced, CPU-only: pretraining a ~5M-param GRU LM on 200k SMILES and all fine-tuning arms are small; all chemistry/descriptor work is RDKit-CPU. Rough planning estimate [est, not measured]: ~1\\u20133 CPU-days pretraining per seed; hours per fine-tuning arm; descriptor/Tanimoto passes over 10\\u2075\\u00d710\\u00b3 comparisons reducible via folded-bit matrices to hours.\\n- Two **flagged speculative dependencies**: PR6 pretrained checkpoint and PR7 learned affinity predictor (plus PR8, optional). Each, if unprovided, is recorded as a limitation; primary conclusions depend only on PR1\\u2013PR5.\\n- Optional degraded **pure-Python smoke rehearsal** (hand-rolled SMILES checks only) may be offered to validate pipelines/harness plumbing, with the standing caveat that re-implemented p-logP/QED are **not comparable** to RDKit reference values and no science conclusions may come from it.\\n\\n## 12. Reporting skeleton\\nPer (target, arm, seed): full metric distributions (not means alone); headline table = family-level contrasts A1\\u2212A0, A1\\u2212A2, A1\\u2212A3; panels for A4 components, A1\\u2032 transfer, weighting grid, scaffold-disjoint reference sensitivity; artifact histograms (chain-run, chain-length vs corpus tail); shape plots; explicit denominator/exclusion table (\\u00a78) reproduced in outputs.\\n\\n## Assumptions vs. fixed requirements\\n- Fixed by the task/rulings: design-only; ChEMBL-versioned corpus+reference; similarity-transfer affinity primary; from-scratch primary generator; composite hallucination battery with retained denominators; distributional diversity trio at fixed K; option-(b) prerequisites; no docking claims.\\n- Assumptions (changeable, labelled): GRU char-LM as generator class; reward-weighted self-distillation with fixed KL as the loop mechanism; the specific target IDs, pChEMBL \\u2265 6 / |A_t| \\u2265 100 cutoffs, K/N/U sizes, L* = 99.5th percentile, the 5-point weighting grid, non-inferiority margins in seed-SD units, and decision-rule CI conventions \\u2014 all are a-priori design choices to be frozen before any run.\\n- Open provisioning uncertainties: exact pinned versions; whether PR6/PR7/PR8 will actually be supplied.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository/environment observations grounding the feasibility and prerequisite sections: (1) /workspace contains only task.json (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\") \\u2014 no code, model, data, or reward implementation exists, so PR1\\u2013PR8 are declared prerequisites, not references to existing artifacts. (2) Import checks: rdkit, numpy, torch, pandas, scipy all ModuleNotFoundError; pip list shows no cheminformatics/ML/docking packages; no obabel/vina; /opt and /srv absent; no pip cache. (3) Network probe failed at DNS resolution and pip download failed \\u2014 environment cannot self-provision, so absence of PR6/PR7 is a limitation pathway in the design, not an implicit assumption. (4) 224 CPU cores, no GPU \\u2014 CPU-only compute-matching protocol and small-model sizing follow from this. Each researcher ruling maps into the design: D1\\u2192\\u00a75 similarity-transfer spec (ECFP4 r2/2048, pChEMBL\\u22656, |A_t|\\u2265100 exclusion, deterministic tie-break) + speculative PR7 secondary + target panel incl. target-agnostic arm; D2\\u2192\\u00a74 molecule-disjoint reference + scaffold-disjoint sensitivity + optional GDB; D3\\u2192\\u00a73/\\u00a76 from-scratch primary with A1p robustness triplet and recorded baseline-rate caveat; D4\\u2192\\u00a78 composite battery with per-metric denominator table retaining unparseable outputs; D5\\u2192\\u00a78 distributional trio at fixed K across seeds; D6\\u2192\\u00a72/\\u00a711 option-(b) pinned prerequisites + smoke-test caveat. Compute-matching is \\u00a77's four numbered protocol rules; weighting sensitivity is \\u00a79; pre-registered outcome patterns (incl. null and mixed) are \\u00a710. No results exist because nothing was executed; all quantities marked [est] are planning values.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Design-only: the deliverable is a frozen protocol; no arm has been run and no performance quantity in this document is an observation.\", \"PR1\\u2013PR5 (pinned RDKit, CPU PyTorch, versioned ChEMBL extract, derived splits and target activity lists) will be provisioned in some external CPU environment; the design is not constrained to the current bare container.\", \"Generator class (GRU char-LM), loop mechanism (reward-weighted self-distillation with fixed KL), and all a-priori constants (target IDs, actives cutoffs, K, N, U, M, L*, weighting grid, non-inferiority margins) are researcher-side design choices to be frozen pre-run, not task requirements.\", \"The similarity-transfer proxy is accepted as an affinity stand-in with the explicit validity limitation (resemblance to known actives \\u2260 physical binding); no docking outcome is claimed anywhere.\", \"If PR6 (pretrained checkpoint) or PR7 (learned affinity predictor) is not supplied, the corresponding arms are recorded as limitations; primary conclusions rest only on PR1\\u2013PR5.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact pinned versions of RDKit/PyTorch/ChEMBL and the final ChEMBL release are unspecified until provisioning; corpus and reference sizes are planning estimates subject to the pinned release's molecule counts.\", \"Whether PR6/PR7/PR8 will actually be provided; their absence removes the prior-strength robustness panel and the secondary affinity arm (recorded as limitations).\", \"Baseline hallucination rate of the from-scratch generator is unknown; if it is near-zero the H-family contrast loses power and if near-total it may floor the property metrics \\u2014 the pre-registered decision rules handle these as null/mixed patterns rather than by post-hoc threshold changes.\", \"Target panel IDs are named as likely-available examples (CHEMBL216/203/257) and must be confirmed against the pinned extract; any target failing the |A_t|\\u2265100 rule is replaced or the panel shrinks, weakening the multi-target generalisation claim.\", \"The declared compute estimates are unmeasured; wall-clock feasibility in the eventual environment should be re-checked at provisioning, though the small-model sizing makes order-of-magnitude overrun unlikely.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-2b9ad743-9a5b-4828-bd85-6ca154b34636", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "end_researcher_turn: {\"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# DESIGN-ONLY DELIVERABLE \\u2014 Does an embedded chemical-feedback loop (p-logP + QED + affinity proxy) improve targeted molecule generation beyond filtering, without sacrificing diversity or real-world distribution alignment?\\n\\nNo experiment has been run. No numbers below are results; every quantity marked [est] is a planning estimate and every threshold is a pre-registered decision rule, not an observation.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Rationale and causal logic\\n\\nThe question conflates three separable claims: (P) feedback improves property attainment; (H) feedback reduces molecular hallucination; (D/A) feedback preserves diversity and aligns output with real drug-like distributions rather than degenerating into artifacts (e.g., ultra-long aliphatic chains). A naive A0-vs-A1 comparison cannot attribute any of these to the *loop*, because A1 typically differs from A0 in sampling compute, gradient updates, and implicit property selection \\u2014 all of which independently move every metric. The design therefore centers two isolating controls:\\n\\n- **A2 (rejection filter on the same R)** answers: is A1's gain indistinguishable from post-hoc selection against the same property functions at matched output properties? A2 shares A1's reward, output size, and (as far as possible) property profile but has no change to the generator's learned distribution.\\n- **A3 (null-reward loop)** answers: do A1's changes survive when the fine-tuning signal is reward-shaped noise matched in distribution? A3 shares A1's exact compute, update count, and distribution-shift mechanics, minus the information content of R.\\n\\nThe feedback loop is credited only for effects that survive **both** contrasts. All other arms decompose attribution (components, weightings, model prior strength, targets vs. target-agnostic transfer).\\n\\n## 2. Declared prerequisites (nothing exists in the current container; see \\u00a710)\\n\\n| ID | Artifact | Spec / pin | Role | Cost [est] |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| PR1 | RDKit | single pinned release (fixed at provisioning, e.g. a 2024\\u20132025.x pip wheel) | validity, descriptors, ECFP4, Murcko, canonical SMILES | wheel, ~100 MB |\\n| PR2 | PyTorch CPU | pinned CPU wheel | training/inference | wheel, ~200 MB |\\n| PR3 | ChEMBL extract | versioned (e.g. v34.x) SMILES + standardised activities + pChEMBL/assay-confidence fields; standardisation protocol fixed (salt-strip, neutralisation, single largest organic fragment, RDKit sanitize, duplicate-by-inchikey) | training corpus, reference, activity annotation | sqlite/CSV, ~50\\u2013200 MB |\\n| PR4 | Corpus split files | fixed random seed; see \\u00a74 | corpus hygiene | derived |\\n| PR5 | Target panel activity lists | derived from PR3 per \\u00a75 | affinity proxy | derived |\\n| PR6 (optional, **speculative-dep #1**) | pretrained checkpoint | GCPN/GENTRL-class or a published ChEMBL-pretrained SMILES LM | D3 robustness arm | weights, ~10\\u2013500 MB |\\n| PR7 (optional, **speculative-dep #2**) | learned affinity predictor + its training tables | small MPNN/GBM on ECFP + target fingerprint, trained on PR3 activities, scaffold-split validation reported | secondary affinity arm | derivable from PR3 but fidelity limited |\\n| PR8 (optional) | GDB-17-style subset | e.g. 10\\u2075 sampled GDB-13/17 molecules | secondary reference for synthesizability-vs-druglikeness separation | file, ~10\\u201350 MB |\\n\\nPR6/PR7 absence is recorded as a **limitation, never imputed as a result** (\\u00a711).\\n\\n## 3. Generator and feedback loop (primary, from scratch per D3)\\n\\n- **G\\u03b8**: 2-layer GRU character LM over canonical-SMILES characters, ~5M params [est], vocab from corpus. CPU-trainable: pretraining on 200k molecules, AdamW, batch 256, until val NLL plateaus; 3 pretraining seeds [est 1\\u20133 days/seed on 32\\u201364 of 224 available threads].\\n- **Composite reward**: R(m) = clip(w1\\u00b7s_plogP + w2\\u00b7QED + w3\\u00b7s_aff, 0, 1); s_plogP = Gaussian target-window score around a fixed logP target (e.g., window centred on the corpus median, width fixed in advance); invalid m \\u2192 R = 0, retained in all loop denominators.\\n- **Feedback injection (fixed choice)**: reward-weighted self-distillation fine-tuning \\u2014 draw M candidates per update, gradient on \\u2212\\u03a3_i softmax(R_i/T)\\u00b7log p(cand_i) with fixed temperature T and fixed KL penalty (\\u03b2 fixed a priori) to the base policy. KL is declared *part of the loop*, not a control; the no-KL variant is an exploratory side condition only.\\n\\n## 4. Corpus, split, and reference hygiene (D2)\\n\\n- Training corpus: fixed-size sample (e.g., 200k [est]) of standardised ChEMBL drug-like molecules (MW 200\\u2013500, heavy atoms \\u2264 45 filters fixed in advance).\\n- **Reference set**: 50k molecules disjoint from training at the molecule level (same standardisation, same size filter) \\u2014 used for all alignment metrics so agreement cannot be inflated by memorised molecules.\\n- **Scaffold-disjoint sensitivity variant**: recompute alignment with a Murcko-scaffold-disjoint reference (and matching scaffold-disjoint training subset) \\u2014 reported as a sensitivity panel, because molecule-disjoint but scaffold-overlapping references can flatter a corpus-trained model.\\n- PR8 (optional) serves as a second reference to separate \\\"looks drug-like\\\" (ChEMBL) from \\\"looks synthesizable-enumerable\\\" (GDB).\\n\\n## 5. Targets and affinity proxy (D1 \\u2014 primary: similarity transfer)\\n\\n- **Panel**: 2\\u20133 activity-annotated targets of the DRD2/EGFR class (e.g., DRD2 = CHEMBL216, EGFR = CHEMBL203, adenosine A2A = CHEMBL257; final IDs fixed from the pinned PR3), plus **one target-agnostic property-optimisation condition** (w3 term dropped or replaced by corpus-wide \\\"drug-likeness similarity\\\" \\u2014 pre-declared: w3 dropped) as the transfer check. At least one genuine target-conditioned arm runs the full contrast \\u2014 required by the question.\\n- **Known-actives set A_t**: ChEMBL activities with assay confidence \\u2265 6, direct-type assays (B/F), pChEMBL \\u2265 6.0; deduplicated molecules; capped at 2,000 largest-potency representatives per target. **If |A_t| < 100 after filtering, target t is excluded from the panel and the exclusion reported.**\\n- **s_aff(m; t)** = max Tanimoto(ECFP4(m), ECFP4(a)) over a \\u2208 A_t. ECFP4 = Morgan radius 2, 2048 bits, RDKit defaults, chirality off, fixed a priori. Invalid m \\u2192 s_aff undefined \\u2192 contributes via R=0 rule. Ties: irrelevant to max; for any top-K selection, ties broken by ascending canonical SMILES (deterministic).\\n- **Secondary/speculative**: PR7 learned predictor as s_aff; **no headline conclusion loads on it**; if PR7 absent, the similarity-transfer result stands with the stated proxy-validity limitation (\\\"proxy rewards structural resemblance to known actives, not physical binding\\\"). **No docking is performed or claimed.**\\n\\n## 6. Arms\\n\\n| Arm | Description | What it isolates |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **A0** | Base checkpoint + U reward-free self-training updates (identical pipeline to A1; candidates drawn identically but *uniformly* selected, no R) | extra gradient steps / self-training drift / decode budget |\\n| **A1** | Full feedback loop (R = w\\u00b7(p-logP, QED, s_aff)) | the loop |\\n| **A2** | A0 generator, N_pool draws, keep top-K by the *same* R; invalid excluded from ranking but counted (\\u00a78 table) | feedback \\u2248 filtering? |\\n| **A3** | A1 pipeline with R replaced by per-sample-permuted A1-reward values (identical weight distribution, zero information) | reward information vs. mechanics |\\n| **A4a/A4b** | Loop with (w1,w2,0) property-only / (0,0,1)-style affinity-only | component attribution |\\n| **A1p** (conditional on PR6) | Pretrained-checkpoint version of A0/A1/A2 triplet | prior-strength robustness (D3) |\\n| **A1\\u2032** | Target-agnostic condition (w3 = 0, no target) | \\\"targeted\\\" vs generic property optimisation |\\n| Grid G | A1/A2 re-run under \\u00a79 weightings | researcher-choice sensitivity |\\n\\n## 7. Compute-matching protocol (explicit, per additional requirement)\\n\\n1. **Decode budget**: every arm draws exactly N = 100,000 candidate molecules [est] per (seed, target) for final evaluation; A1's training draws are logged separately.\\n2. **Gradient updates**: A0 and A3 execute the *same* U updates, batch size, optimiser state, LR schedule, and candidate draws M per update as A1; only the selection weights differ (uniform / permuted / R-weighted).\\n3. **A2 cost logging**: N_pool required to fill top-K is logged per arm; A2's N_pool is additionally matched to A1's total training draws (with replacement noted if pool exhausted). A reviewer can therefore see A2 gets \\u2265 A1's sampling compute, and A0/A3 get A1's full update count.\\n4. All arms share RNG streams, decoding temperature, and the same fixed output size **K = 10,000** [est] molecules (D5 fixed-K subsampling; deterministic seed).\\n\\n## 8. Metrics, denominators, and exclusion rules (D4/D5 \\u2014 no arm may shrink its own denominator)\\n\\n| Family | Metrics | Denominator policy (fixed) |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Property (P) | QED, SA (RDKit sascorer), p-logP window score, composite R, success-rate at pre-set thresholds | reported on **all K outputs**, invalid scored 0; secondary valid-only view shown side-by-side |\\n| Hallucination (H) | (i) parse/sanitisation/canonicalisation failure rate; (ii) valence & ring-size (3\\u20138) violations; (iii) duplicate rate post-canonicalisation (uniqueness); (iv) off-distribution rate: log-frequency under corpus fragment (fixed-size circular fragments) and generic-Murcko-scaffold frequency models \\u2014 molecule scored by mean min-log-prob; (v) artifact detector: max contiguous aliphatic-C run \\u2265 L*, L* = corpus 99.5th percentile fixed from PR3 before any arm runs | **all K outputs, always**; unparseable outputs retained (they *are* the hallucination signal) |\\n| Diversity (D) | ECFP4 NN-Tanimoto distance distribution, internal diversity (mean pairwise Tanimoto complement), generic-scaffold count + Shannon entropy of scaffold distribution | fixed-K samples; distributions reported, never a lone scalar |\\n| Alignment (A) | FDD-style descriptor-distribution distance vs reference; Morgan-density and scaffold JS divergence; principal-moments-of-inertia shape plot vs reference; chain-length, heavy-atom, ring-count histograms vs reference tails | fixed-K samples vs fixed reference (\\u00a74) |\\n\\n**Caveat (required, D3/D4):** with a from-scratch generator, baseline invalid/off-distribution rates are expected to be high, giving the loop visible headroom; the A1p sensitivity triplet and explicitly reported baseline rates let the reader judge how much of any \\\"gain\\\" is headroom exploitation. If PR6 is unavailable, this remains a limitation, not a result.\\n\\n## 9. Weighting sensitivity (w1/w2/w3 is a researcher choice \\u2014 probed, not hidden)\\n\\nPre-registered grid of 5 weightings: (\\u2153,\\u2153,\\u2153) primary; (.2,.5,.3); (.3,.2,.5); (.5,.3,.2); (.1,.3,.6) [affinity-heavy]. Headline contrast patterns (below) are recomputed per weighting; the headline conclusion is only declared *stable* if its category is unchanged in \\u2265 4/5 weightings; otherwise the conclusion is reported as weighting-dependent.\\n\\n## 10. Pre-registered decision criteria (patterns; no prediction of which obtains)\\n\\nAll contrasts per (seed, target) across 5 training seeds [est]; seed-level paired bootstrap/permutation tests (p < 0.05, BH-corrected across families) with effect sizes and seed SDs reported. Let \\u0394(X) denote arm X \\u2212 baseline on a metric family.\\n\\n- **\\\"Loop adds something beyond filtering\\\"**: \\u0394(A1\\u2212A0) favours A1 on H and (P), **and** \\u0394(A1\\u2212A2) is positive on \\u2265 1 alignment metric and on off-distribution rate with CI excluding 0, **and** \\u0394(A1\\u2212A3) favours A1 on H \\u2014 i.e., gains not reproduced by same-reward filtering or same-mechanics noise \\u2014 **and** diversity trio for A1 non-inferior to A0 (NN-Tanimoto and scaffold entropy CIs within a pre-set non-inferiority margin of seed SD).\\n- **\\\"Loop \\u2261 filtering\\\"**: A2 \\u2248 A1 on all four families (all CIs crossing 0), with both beating A0/A3. The loop's extra machinery buys nothing over ranking.\\n- **\\\"Loop degrades diversity/alignment\\\"**: A1 wins (P) and possibly (H) but fails the diversity non-inferiority clause or shows alignment regression (e.g., scaffold entropy collapse, chain-run tail vs corpus) \\u2014 including any ultra-long-chain artifact spike in A1 but not A2 (signature of reward hacking).\\n- **\\\"Null\\\"**: A1 \\u2248 A0 on (P) and (H) across seeds.\\n- **\\\"Mixed\\\"**: any pattern outside the above four; reported as-is with the failing contrast named. Weighting sensitivity (\\u00a79) and A1p (if available) qualify the category, never overwrite it.\\n\\n## 11. Feasibility (explicit)\\n\\n- **Verified absent in the current container** (inspection, 2026-10-23): RDKit, numpy/scipy/pandas/torch, any docking/scoring tool, any dataset or checkpoint, pip cache, and *network access itself* (DNS resolution fails; pip download fails). Python 3.14 only, CPU-only (224 cores, no GPU). **Nothing in this design was executed here, and none of it is executable here as-is.**\\n- Runnable elsewhere as specced, CPU-only: pretraining a ~5M-param GRU LM on 200k SMILES and all fine-tuning arms are small; all chemistry/descriptor work is RDKit-CPU. Rough planning estimate [est, not measured]: ~1\\u20133 CPU-days pretraining per seed; hours per fine-tuning arm; descriptor/Tanimoto passes over 10\\u2075\\u00d710\\u00b3 comparisons reducible via folded-bit matrices to hours.\\n- Two **flagged speculative dependencies**: PR6 pretrained checkpoint and PR7 learned affinity predictor (plus PR8, optional). Each, if unprovided, is recorded as a limitation; primary conclusions depend only on PR1\\u2013PR5.\\n- Optional degraded **pure-Python smoke rehearsal** (hand-rolled SMILES checks only) may be offered to validate pipelines/harness plumbing, with the standing caveat that re-implemented p-logP/QED are **not comparable** to RDKit reference values and no science conclusions may come from it.\\n\\n## 12. Reporting skeleton\\nPer (target, arm, seed): full metric distributions (not means alone); headline table = family-level contrasts A1\\u2212A0, A1\\u2212A2, A1\\u2212A3; panels for A4 components, A1\\u2032 transfer, weighting grid, scaffold-disjoint reference sensitivity; artifact histograms (chain-run, chain-length vs corpus tail); shape plots; explicit denominator/exclusion table (\\u00a78) reproduced in outputs.\\n\\n## Assumptions vs. fixed requirements\\n- Fixed by the task/rulings: design-only; ChEMBL-versioned corpus+reference; similarity-transfer affinity primary; from-scratch primary generator; composite hallucination battery with retained denominators; distributional diversity trio at fixed K; option-(b) prerequisites; no docking claims.\\n- Assumptions (changeable, labelled): GRU char-LM as generator class; reward-weighted self-distillation with fixed KL as the loop mechanism; the specific target IDs, pChEMBL \\u2265 6 / |A_t| \\u2265 100 cutoffs, K/N/U sizes, L* = 99.5th percentile, the 5-point weighting grid, non-inferiority margins in seed-SD units, and decision-rule CI conventions \\u2014 all are a-priori design choices to be frozen before any run.\\n- Open provisioning uncertainties: exact pinned versions; whether PR6/PR7/PR8 will actually be supplied.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository/environment observations grounding the feasibility and prerequisite sections: (1) /workspace contains only task.json (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\") \\u2014 no code, model, data, or reward implementation exists, so PR1\\u2013PR8 are declared prerequisites, not references to existing artifacts. (2) Import checks: rdkit, numpy, torch, pandas, scipy all ModuleNotFoundError; pip list shows no cheminformatics/ML/docking packages; no obabel/vina; /opt and /srv absent; no pip cache. (3) Network probe failed at DNS resolution and pip download failed \\u2014 environment cannot self-provision, so absence of PR6/PR7 is a limitation pathway in the design, not an implicit assumption. (4) 224 CPU cores, no GPU \\u2014 CPU-only compute-matching protocol and small-model sizing follow from this. Each researcher ruling maps into the design: D1\\u2192\\u00a75 similarity-transfer spec (ECFP4 r2/2048, pChEMBL\\u22656, |A_t|\\u2265100 exclusion, deterministic tie-break) + speculative PR7 secondary + target panel incl. target-agnostic arm; D2\\u2192\\u00a74 molecule-disjoint reference + scaffold-disjoint sensitivity + optional GDB; D3\\u2192\\u00a73/\\u00a76 from-scratch primary with A1p robustness triplet and recorded baseline-rate caveat; D4\\u2192\\u00a78 composite battery with per-metric denominator table retaining unparseable outputs; D5\\u2192\\u00a78 distributional trio at fixed K across seeds; D6\\u2192\\u00a72/\\u00a711 option-(b) pinned prerequisites + smoke-test caveat. Compute-matching is \\u00a77's four numbered protocol rules; weighting sensitivity is \\u00a79; pre-registered outcome patterns (incl. null and mixed) are \\u00a710. No results exist because nothing was executed; all quantities marked [est] are planning values.\", \"assumptions\": [\"Design-only: the deliverable is a frozen protocol; no arm has been run and no performance quantity in this document is an observation.\", \"PR1\\u2013PR5 (pinned RDKit, CPU PyTorch, versioned ChEMBL extract, derived splits and target activity lists) will be provisioned in some external CPU environment; the design is not constrained to the current bare container.\", \"Generator class (GRU char-LM), loop mechanism (reward-weighted self-distillation with fixed KL), and all a-priori constants (target IDs, actives cutoffs, K, N, U, M, L*, weighting grid, non-inferiority margins) are researcher-side design choices to be frozen pre-run, not task requirements.\", \"The similarity-transfer proxy is accepted as an affinity stand-in with the explicit validity limitation (resemblance to known actives \\u2260 physical binding); no docking outcome is claimed anywhere.\", \"If PR6 (pretrained checkpoint) or PR7 (learned affinity predictor) is not supplied, the corresponding arms are recorded as limitations; primary conclusions rest only on PR1\\u2013PR5.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Exact pinned versions of RDKit/PyTorch/ChEMBL and the final ChEMBL release are unspecified until provisioning; corpus and reference sizes are planning estimates subject to the pinned release's molecule counts.\", \"Whether PR6/PR7/PR8 will actually be provided; their absence removes the prior-strength robustness panel and the secondary affinity arm (recorded as limitations).\", \"Baseline hallucination rate of the from-scratch generator is unknown; if it is near-zero the H-family contrast loses power and if near-total it may floor the property metrics \\u2014 the pre-registered decision rules handle these as null/mixed patterns rather than by post-hoc threshold changes.\", \"Target panel IDs are named as likely-available examples (CHEMBL216/203/257) and must be confirmed against the pinned extract; any target failing the |A_t|\\u2265100 rule is replaced or the panel shrinks, weakening the multi-target generalisation claim.\", \"The declared compute estimates are unmeasured; wall-clock feasibility in the eventual environment should be re-checked at provisioning, though the small-model sizing makes order-of-magnitude overrun unlikely.\"]}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
